# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Dependencies
node_modules/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Build output
dist/
build/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Exception: the app's dependency-free deploy tree is committed on purpose so the
# app can be deployed straight from Git via the Databricks Apps UI (Source code
# path = player-insights-agent/build/deploy). It has no package.json, so the
# platform skips npm install. See player-insights-agent/.gitignore for the full
# note. Rebuild with `npm run build:deploy` (in player-insights-agent/) and
# recommit to update it.
!player-insights-agent/build/
player-insights-agent/build/*
!player-insights-agent/build/deploy/
!player-insights-agent/build/deploy/**

# Local MLflow state. mlflow.db holds traced prompts and answers.
mlruns/
mlflow.db

# Rendered documents. The leak check cannot review a PDF, so it cannot clear one.
docs/*.pdf

# Design-handoff screenshots, for the same reason one step further on: a PNG can
# neither be scanned by the leak check nor rewritten by publish-rewrite.pl, so
# whatever is drawn in one is drawn in it permanently. The answer-card screen in
# the astrolabe bundles renders the customer's own title roster into a chart, a
# breakdown and a caveat list -- the exact strings mirror/publish-rewrite.pl
# exists to replace in text -- and two others show a Databricks address inside a
# GRANT and a signed-in username. Held out on 2026-08-17 as a class rather than
# per file, because bundles 4, 5 and 6 all carried them and the next one will.
#
# They are reference material for building the surfaces, not something the app
# needs, so nothing is lost by reading them from where the bundle is unpacked.
# docs/design-handoff-astrolabe/SCREENSHOTS.md says where that is.
docs/**/screens2/
docs/**/screenshots/

# Release certificates. A certificate names the workspace, the app, the endpoint,
# the Lakebase branch and every table in the manifest, and the publication
# rewrite is a line-wise pass that cannot remove a document. Point
# bundle/certify-release.sh --store at shared storage to share them.
.certificates/

# Test and audit artifacts
.ui-test-artifacts/
.approval-repro/
playwright-report/
test-results/
coverage/

# Ad-hoc probe and scratch output dropped at the repo root while investigating,
# by a person or by an agent. Whatever the investigation was about ends up inside
# them: .audit-probe.json, the one that prompted this entry, holds a live SQL
# warehouse id and a `system.access.audit` query. Nobody's deliverable, nobody's
# job to tidy up, and one careless `git add .` away from being committed -- which
# is exactly the accident that puts an identifier into a tracked file and then
# into a publication.
#
# ROOT-ANCHORED with a leading slash, deliberately. `*-probe.json` unanchored
# would also hide a deliberate test fixture somewhere down the tree, and a
# .gitignore that swallows files people meant to commit gets deleted by the next
# person it confuses. Add a name here rather than widening the patterns.
/.audit-probe.json
/*-probe.json
/*.probe.json
/*-scratch.json
/scratch/

# Local tooling
.DS_Store
*.log
# One editor's own reminder state, written into the repository root. Nothing
# reads it here, and it is named rather than pattern-matched because this repo
# publishes: an untracked, unignored file at the root is one `git add -A` away
# from being committed, and from there sync-mirror.sh copies it to a public
# repository along with whoever's machine it came from.
/.isaac/
